CURRENT POST-UPDATE VALIDITY MARGIN

After the existing
current signed-B update,
define:

M_post_current(i,s)

=
aligned_margin(
B_current(i),
s
).

This already-existing
post-update signed state
is read only
for the A53 veto.

No new state variable exists.

No magnitude threshold exists.

VALID_CURRENT_COMMITMENT

valid(i,s)

iff:

M_post_current(i,s) > 0.

Invalid iff:

M_post_current(i,s) <= 0.

TAU0 CONTROL

Decision pressure:

PRESSURE_decision
=
PRESSURE_now.

Exact A52 TAU0.

TAU3_FIXED CONTROL

Preserve exact A52 TAU3.

If uninterrupted
same-side pressure history
contains the exact
three-epoch-old source:

PRESSURE_decision
=
PRESSURE_now(t-3).

Otherwise:

PRESSURE_decision
=
PRESSURE_now(t).

No veto.

TAU3_VETO TREATMENT

If:

valid(i,s) = TRUE

AND

the exact uninterrupted
same-side t-3 history exists:

PRESSURE_decision
=
PRESSURE_now(t-3).

Otherwise:

PRESSURE_decision
=
PRESSURE_now(t).

Thus:

current post-update
signed evidence
can cancel phase memory.

The veto does not:

modify B;

modify stored pressure history;

modify cooperative echo;

modify recruitment;

modify push-pull;

modify action randomness;

or create a new commitment state.

PRESSURE HISTORY

Preserve A52:

store current PRESSURE_now only.

Never store delayed pressure.

Never store veto-selected pressure.

History remains side-specific.

History resets on:

defection;

refractory;

U;

H;

side change;

loss of commitment.

Warm-up uses current pressure.

No future read.

No recursive delayed history.

