FAILURE ATTRIBUTION

If veto restores
old-majority loss <=4

but destroys
the TAU3 burst-end benefit:

the useful phase effect
requires stale persistence
beyond the point
current evidence still validates it.

Do not weaken the veto
post-result.

If veto preserves
most TAU3 burst benefit
and restores reversal safety
but macro thresholds remain weak:

a safe local phase primitive exists,
but this periodic benchmark
still does not justify
further mechanism tuning.

Freeze the primitive
as optional
and move to Task 1.

If veto restores safety
and materially suppresses
the macro oscillator:

retain TAU3_VETO
as a validated developmental primitive.

Move to Task 1.

If veto does not
restore reversal safety:

current signed evidence
is insufficient
to validate phase memory.

Do not add another phase heuristic.

Move to Task 1.

If veto is mechanically inactive:

the diagnostic seam
does not transfer
to fresh worlds.

Move to Task 1.

